[2026-03-08T16:46:31.416Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node] • Yes. The better move is to port Aurora’s ideas, not Aurora’s selectors.
[2026-03-08T16:46:31.416Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node] 
[2026-03-08T16:46:31.416Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]   What I’d do for Aether instead:
[2026-03-08T16:46:31.416Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node] 
[2026-03-08T16:46:31.416Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]   1. Build an Aether-native surface tagger in content.js.
[2026-03-08T16:46:31.416Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]      Use a small runtime classifier that tags dynamic nodes with data-aether-surface="tooltip|
[2026-03-08T16:46:31.416Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]      menu|toast|search-panel|source-chip" and data-aether-glass="passive|raised|interactive".
[2026-03-08T16:46:31.416Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]      That is much better than chasing ChatGPT’s transient class names in CSS forever. › Improve documentation in @filename   gpt-5.4 xhigh · 26% left · ~/Documents/GitHub/Aether
[2026-03-08T16:46:31.416Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]   2. Style by semantic surface, not by raw wrapper classes, in styles.css.
[2026-03-08T16:46:31.416Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]      Aether already has good glass tokens like passive/raised/interactive. We should extend
[2026-03-08T16:46:31.416Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]      that system to:
[2026-03-08T16:46:31.416Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node] 
[2026-03-08T16:46:31.416Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]   - tooltip
[2026-03-08T16:46:31.416Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]   - toast
[2026-03-08T16:46:31.416Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]   - source-chip
[2026-03-08T16:46:31.416Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]   - search-results
[2026-03-08T16:46:31.416Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]   - ephemeral-popover
[2026-03-08T16:46:31.416Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]     Then most CSS becomes stable and readable:
[2026-03-08T16:46:31.416Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]     [data-aether-surface="tooltip"] { ... }
[2026-03-08T16:46:31.416Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]     instead of long one-off selectors.
[2026-03-08T16:46:34.401Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node] 
[2026-03-08T16:46:34.401Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node] 
[2026-03-08T16:46:34.401Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]   3. Keep static selectors only for truly stable anchors.
[2026-03-08T16:46:34.401Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]      Good examples:
[2026-03-08T16:46:34.401Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node] 
[2026-03-08T16:46:34.401Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]   - [role="tooltip"]
[2026-03-08T16:46:34.401Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]   - [role="alert"]
[2026-03-08T16:46:34.401Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]   - [role="status"]
[2026-03-08T16:46:34.401Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]   - [role="menu"]
[2026-03-08T16:46:34.401Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]   - [role="listbox"]
[2026-03-08T16:46:34.401Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]   - [data-testid="stage-thread-flyout"]
[2026-03-08T16:46:34.401Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]     Bad examples:
[2026-03-08T16:46:34.401Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]   - giant Tailwind class soups
[2026-03-08T16:46:34.401Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]   - brittle wrapper chains
[2026-03-08T16:46:34.401Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]   - copied selectors that only happen to work today
[2026-03-08T16:46:34.401Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node] 
[2026-03-08T16:46:34.401Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]   4. Add a tiny “overlay discovery” observer.
[2026-03-08T16:46:34.401Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]      Aurora’s best idea is its dynamic tagging pass. For Aether, I’d make that smaller and
[2026-03-08T16:46:34.401Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]      cleaner:
[2026-03-08T16:46:34.401Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node] 
[2026-03-08T16:46:34.401Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]   - watch added nodes
[2026-03-08T16:46:34.401Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]   - if node or ancestor matches a stable overlay heuristic, tag it
[2026-03-08T16:46:37.401Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node] 
