[2026-03-08T17:44:54.590Z] [out] [id=1] [terminal=node] 
[2026-03-08T17:44:54.590Z] [out] [id=1] [terminal=node]   - Medium: the embedded report shell is stretching the iframe host much wider than the report content can
[2026-03-08T17:44:54.590Z] [out] [id=1] [terminal=node]     actually use. The host framing rules in styles.css:2384 and styles.css:2392 force a full-width padded frame
[2026-03-08T17:44:54.590Z] [out] [id=1] [terminal=node]     around a cross-origin iframe. In your first screenshot, that shows up as the huge empty left and right gutters
[2026-03-08T17:44:54.590Z] [out] [id=1] [terminal=node]     inside the report card. Since the iframe internals stay centered and sandboxed, making the host wider just
[2026-03-08T17:44:54.590Z] [out] [id=1] [terminal=node]     magnifies dead space instead of improving readability.
[2026-03-08T17:44:57.297Z] [out] [id=1] [terminal=node] 
[2026-03-08T17:44:57.297Z] [out] [id=1] [terminal=node]   - Medium: the action buttons are visually inconsistent inside the same surface. The general research-viewer
[2026-03-08T17:44:57.297Z] [out] [id=1] [terminal=node]     rules only skin download/share/close in styles.css:2253, while the iframe-host-specific rules only skin
